WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-So nice to be back.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.302 line:92%
-I'm thrilled to have you back.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:05.705
Now, last time you were here,
you were about to host "SNL."

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
It was the last time, yeah.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With U2.
And you were talking about how

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.678
you had taken your mother to see
"Lady Bird" in the theater.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:12.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And you were very nervous

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.614
about getting recognized,
and no one recognized you.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No one recognized me.
No. Nobody.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:17.684 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.786 size:81% position:41%
-And yet here you are.
It did not get to you.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:20.653 line:92%
That did not sink your spirit.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No it's not --
it's not a big deal.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
You just pushed right through.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I'm fine.
Um, I'm fine.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good.
I can tell.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:31.364
But now, have you taken your
mother to see this film yet?

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.198 line:92%
Have you taken her to see it?

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I took her to the New York
premiere of this film,

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:40.373
so everyone had to recognize me.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why take chances?
-Do you know what I mean?

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:45.712
-Yeah.
-There were posters everywhere.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would, like,
stand next to them.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.783 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"That's me in that."

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it really impressed her,
I think.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:54.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's a -- There's a lot
of wigs and a lot of --

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always feel bad,
because this is obviously --

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're playing --
you and Margot Robbie both

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
are playing
these really powerful women,

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:03.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
but because of the age
it takes place, so much wigs.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
So many corsets.
-Yeah, a lot of corsets.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:10.537
And when you've been wearing
them, like we did, for months,

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
you take them off
at the end of the job,

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like,
your shape has changed.

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:16.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I didn't
have any curves before.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:20.580 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And then I took it off,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
and for about a month,
I was like, "Oh."

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-"Wow, look at that."

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then is about a month
when it goes back to --

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Went back to...
-Yeah.

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:32.559 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, there you go.
Wow.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
It never occurred to me
that it worked.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, because it's squishing
you're insides.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:38.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And it's on --

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.901
Like, we'd have it on for,
you know, 12 hours a day.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:42.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And it's tight.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
Corsets are tight.
So when -- yeah.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.774
And so it actually does change
your shape for a little bit.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:48.341 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I don't know.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.976
This has turned into a weird
advertisement for corsets.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:53.780
-Yeah, I feel like --
Yeah, don't -- don't wear them.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.781 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Don't do it.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
Stay in school.
Don't do corsets.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:02.021
You obviously have an incredible
co-star with Margot Robbie.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And there --

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.126 size:84% position:42%
Really late in the film
is the first time --

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.161 size:81% position:41%
You know, obviously,
it's based on history,

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you guys don't meet
until very late in the film.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And it's very powerful,

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
because these two,
you know, women we've seen

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
throughout the film,
we haven't seen them meet.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:17.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And do they actually --

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you guys put some thought
into how much time

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
you should interact as actors
before that scene, yeah?

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we didn't
have any interaction at all.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:28.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we both decided
in rehearsals --

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:30.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I had heard --
We've all heard about actors

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
staying apart
for the whole thing

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:35.255
or being in character and
staying method and all of that.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:39.826
And I've never really felt the
need to do that, necessarily.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.361 line:92%
but with this I just thought --

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.363
For Margot and I,
we knew each other a little bit.

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:46.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
We knew that we sort of worked
in a similar enough way.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we could --
we could kind of go for it.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.838 line:92%
So we rehearsed separately.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:52.872 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We shot separately.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.641 line:92%
She did all of her stuff first.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:57.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
her last day was my first day,

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.111 line:92%
and it was that big scene.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:01.347
So we stayed apart for the whole
first half of the scene

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.883
where we're sort of hidden
behind these sort of sheets

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.786
in a -- in a cabin in the woods
that we're in.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:09.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- And then when --
Or, you know,

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:12.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
physical appearance is finally
revealed to each other.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was actually
the very first time

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.129 line:92%
we saw each other in character.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:19.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I had never seen Margot
with the red wig

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.034 line:92%
and the Golden Age makeup.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.302 line:92%
I hadn't seen any of it at all.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:26.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the first take was us
just being like, "Oh, my God!"

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.307 line:92%
and, like, really emotional.

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, there was a moment,
for those --

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:31.644
You drop the accent,
and you just say, "Holy [bleep]"

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:32.946 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Holy [bleep]

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Jesus, Margot!"
-Yeah.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.950
-"What's wrong with your face?"
-It's jarring.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.151 line:92%
I will say, it's a really --

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It takes you out of it
for a sec.

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:41.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
You won't notice it, really,
though.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
Once you watch it again,
you don't know.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:45.358
-Yeah, but the first time,
you do have a moment of like,

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Did she Irish and call her
'Margot' right there?"

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.495 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it really speaks
to how good you guys are

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.398 size:81% position:41%
that you immediately
go right back into it.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-She's Australian.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.937
And then she's like, "Hi, mate.
How's it going, Mary?"

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:58.972 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:01.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You --
So, you obviously --

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:04.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had to have
a Scottish accent for this.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:06.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Lady Bird," you -- you know,
you're from California.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.682
Your accent -- this --
You came by this very honestly.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it true
that you developed your skill

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
and your ear for accents
because your dolls

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.655
all came from different places?
-Yeah.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:19.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So I am -- I'm an only child.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:20.360 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously. "Aww."
Someone just went "Aww."

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:26.666
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, we thought that, Saoirse.

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.401 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And I would, like --

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:32.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
Basically, I would
visit my dolls every evening

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:33.573 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
like a soap opera.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:36.376
So there would be episodes,
so I'd come back every day,

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:39.545
and I'd be like, "What's
Polly Pocket been up to today?"

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:43.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had this mini figurine
of Woody from "Toy Story"

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:47.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
back when, you know,
fast-food stores

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
used to give out
really good toys.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:51.157 size:78% position:39%
And this was when --
And I still have him,

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:52.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was Polly Pocket's
boyfriend.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
And he -- he was American.

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:58.197
He was, like, generic American.
She was from the South.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:02.201 size:75% position:38%
And she lost her arm
in a car accident.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:02.602 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Really?

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:03.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Because in real life,

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
I actually broke off her arm
by accident.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Got it.
-So I had to rewrite that.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
You had to rewrite in a way

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:13.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you weren't culpable.
-Right. Exactly, yeah.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.047 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:15.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
It actually worked out
really well...

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...for the grit of it all.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, of course.
I mean, I think when you --

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.120
Obviously, when you're
making a doll soap opera,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
you need things to happen.
-You need the drama.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I wanted people to know,

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, this is real life.
This --

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
people lose their arms.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. Because
that's the thing about dolls.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
They live
such sheltered existences.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They do.
Plastic, if you will.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.202 line:92%
-They could go their whole life,

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:37.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they don't even
leave the house.

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:38.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With two arms.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:39.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They have two arms
their whole lives,

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then every other doll
is like,

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, I'm always
gonna have two arms,"

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:43.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's not the case.
-Yeah.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:47.814
And so, if anything, it was a
cautionary tale for the other --

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that you've said,
none of your dolls

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
ever went out
driving again after that.

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:52.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. No.
-Yeah.

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:55.488
-It was -- I'm glad I could just
give something back to them.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:57.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, go see
"Mary Queen of Scots."

00:05:57.924 --> 00:06:00.093 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

